Jerry has 41 regular sodas and 22 diet sodas. First, we calculate the total number of sodas:

$$
41 + 22 = 63
$$

The fridge can hold 9 sodas on each shelf. To find out how many shelves are needed, we divide the total number of sodas by the capacity of each shelf:

$$
63 \div 9 = 7
$$

Thus, Jerry will need to fill up 7 shelves. The final answer is:

$$
\boxed{7}
$$

