$$
48 - 19 = 29
$$

He then used the money earned from selling these 19 books to buy 38 new books. The total number of books he has now is the remaining books plus the new ones he bought:

$$
29 + 38 = 67
$$

Thus, the final answer is:

$$
\boxed{67}
$$

