Now, each player has 8 lives. So, each of these 7 players has 8 lives. To find the total number of lives, I need to multiply the number of players by the number of lives each player has. That would be 7 players times 8 lives per player. Let me do that calculation. 7 multiplied by 8. Hmm, 7 times 8 is 56. Wait, is that right? Let me verify. 7 times 8 is 56. Yes, because 7 times 10 is 70, minus 7 times 2 which is 14, so 70 minus 14 is 56. So that checks out.

